# 1. MISSION

Conduct a comprehensive architectural audit of the entire KhelGrid platform to determine whether its existing architecture can support a scalable, modular, multi-tenant SaaS ecosystem.

This audit must cover the complete platform, not merely the existing SaaS implementation.

We want to establish a reusable SaaS foundation that can eventually support every suitable KhelGrid module.

The architecture must support:

1. Individual users.
2. Athletes.
3. Coaches.
4. Sports academies.
5. Sports venues.
6. Schools and colleges.
7. Universities.
8. Sports clubs.
9. Sports federations.
10. Tournament organizers.
11. Event organizers.
12. Sports associations.
13. Corporate sports organizations.
14. Training and development organizations.
15. Sports service providers.
16. Research and editorial organizations.
17. Future enterprise customers.
18. Platform administrators.
19. Platform moderators.
20. Organization administrators.
21. Organization employees and staff.
22. Organization-specific teams and departments.

The goal is not to create unnecessary complexity.

The goal is to build a strong foundation where new modules can adopt standardized tenancy, permissions, organization ownership and entitlements without repeatedly reinventing these systems.

We want KhelGrid to be capable of evolving into a large sports technology ecosystem.

