# 16. PART M — SAAS SECURITY TESTING GAP ANALYSIS

Inspect all existing tests.

Determine whether the current test suite verifies:

## Tenant isolation

- Tenant A cannot read Tenant B data.
- Tenant A cannot modify Tenant B data.
- Tenant A cannot delete Tenant B data.
- Tenant A cannot insert resources under Tenant B.
- Tenant A cannot change its tenant ownership.
- Cross-tenant joins do not leak information.

## Organization authorization

- Non-members cannot access private organization data.
- Members cannot assign themselves owner permissions.
- Removed members lose access.
- Suspended organizations cannot perform prohibited operations.
- Users can belong to multiple organizations safely.

## Role security

- Organization admin cannot become platform admin.
- Moderator cannot access super-admin controls.
- Read-only roles cannot modify protected records.
- Permissions are checked server-side.

## Subscription and entitlements

- Expired subscriptions lose applicable premium access.
- Cancelled subscriptions follow defined access rules.
- Free features remain accessible.
- Admin overrides are audited.
- Clients cannot forge entitlements.
- Usage limits cannot be bypassed through direct API calls.

## Identity isolation

- Users retain independent personal identities.
- Organization membership does not automatically transfer ownership of personal resources.
- Organization switching cannot expose previous organization data.

Classify every test as:

PASS — verified by actual execution evidence.

FAIL — reproduced failure.

NOT EXECUTED — test exists but was not executed.

MISSING — no corresponding test exists.

NOT VERIFIED — evidence is insufficient.

Do not report a test as passing simply because its source file exists.

